SWEET AMP HAL FORMAT (patch 0176), on top of 0175: boot-arg sweetaoc=10 = sweetaoc=9 plus what the stock HAL sets that 0166 did not. Stock
oriole vendor.img mixer paths (factory CP1A.260405.005) set TDM_0_RX Chan Four / Format S32_LE, so the codec pcm_hw_params gets ASP_WIDTH_RX
32 and ASP_RX_WL 24 (AMP cs35l41.c:2725-2750); 0166 used the card default S16_LE (16 / 16). Also R ASPRX1/2 slot 1/0 (L 0/1), DSP RX2 Source
ASPRX1, AMP PCM Gain 17, speaker-path boost peak 1.70 A L / 1.90 A R. Written once per amp before GLOBAL_EN (SP_ENABLES off); restore() resets
the amps. The diagnostic window gains path-word and CSPL meter lines (BDLOG_MAX_EXC, SPK_OUTPUT_POWER, ... from the wmfw coefficient list)
at snapshots S (silence), A (pattern 4, DSP path), G (gap), B (pattern 5, DSP bypassed), end; patterns 4/5 are 2 s beeps at -12.2 dBFS
and log "SWEET AUDIO: pattern <n> starts now".

